ndicate they are imperial satraps who have internalized the romanticized \"Arab Culture\" created by French, British and, later, American Orientalists; the examples include critical analyses of the colonial literature of Joseph Conrad, which conflates a people, a time, and a place into a narrative of incident and adventure in an exotic land. The critical application of post-structuralism in the scholarship of Orientalism influenced the development of literary theory, cultural criticism, and the field of Middle Eastern studies, especially regarding how academics practice their intellectual inquiry when examining, describing, and explaining the Middle East.","publicationYear":1978,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Study and teaching","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-orientalism-edward-w-said"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"East and West","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-orientalism-edward-w-said"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Foreign public opinion, Occidental","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-orientalism-edward-w-said"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Imperialism","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-orientalism-edward-w-said"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Foreign opinion, Occidental","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-orientalism-edward-w-said"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Orientalism","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-orientalism-edward-w-said"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"History","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-orientalism-edward-w-said"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Foreign public opinion","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-orientalism-edward-w-said"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","la